# Settings the paper bot runs with on this server. deploy/ensure-env.sh writes each KEY=VALUE line below into
# ~/bot/bot.env on every deploy, replacing any line of that name, but only while bot.env's TRADING_MODE is paper (or
# not set: the bot's default is paper). Under shadow or live nothing here is applied, and nothing already in bot.env is
# removed. To change one of these, change it here and deploy; an edit made only in bot.env is put back at the next deploy.
# Plain KEY=VALUE lines only: no quotes, spaces or `export`.

# Tennis two paper days (Steven, Nov 12, 2:41 AM EST / 07:41 UTC: full control overnight, merge and deploy per the plan).
# The tennis lane passed the one test (GitHub run 43164645344) with the momentum signal counted when our player's mid
# rose at least 2c over the last 2 minutes (the defaults: 1c over 1 minute). The two paper days run those settings, on
# ATP and WTA matches. TENNIS_LIVE is not set here: live tennis stays off behind its own switch.
TENNIS_CONF_MOMENTUM_CENTS=0.02
TENNIS_CONF_WINDOW_SEC=120
TENNIS_SERIES=KXATPMATCH,KXWTAMATCH
